From 92a771f2785e0a441e3785d4fd0cd0c583cefaad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 20:30:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic-parallel: finite strain behaviours, initialize
 functions, post-processings and rotations

- finite strain behaviours (standard, Green-Lagrange and Hencky
  strategies), sizes of a point depending on the stress measure and the
  tangent operator;
- batch initialize functions and post-processings, called through function
  objects generated by MFront;
- batch rotation functions of orthotropic behaviours
  (`mfront_gpb_RotationData`, rotation matrix per point or uniform);
- a single primitive per backend, `apply`, used by integration, initialize
  functions, post-processings and rotations; `PointView` copies all the
  inputs in its constructor and reads the outputs through the pointers of
  the behaviour data (works around a wrong code generation of nvcc 13.0);
- material properties of a point include the elastic properties when the
  stiffness tensor is required;
- SYCL: `DeviceCopies` shared by the batch data and the rotations;
- nvcc warnings 20011 and 20014 (calls to host functions in device code)
  are errors in the configurations using nvcc;
- tests: one comparison program and one list of comparisons
  (`compare-all.sh`) for all the configurations, covering finite strain,
  initialize functions, post-processings, rotations, orthotropic and heat
  transfer behaviours, single crystals, energies, speed of sound, Runge-Kutta,
  cohesive zone models and out of bounds policies;
- documentation.
